id: pm-79gv6q
title: "pm context summary counts are denominated in the returned slice, so the canonical orient cold-start reports 4 open items in a 291-item backlog"
description: "Measured 2026-09-04 on the 2026.9.4 build against the live tracker (291 open, 65 blocked, 2631 total). pm context summary reports active_items, open, and blocked denominated in the returned slice, not the workspace: the default limit reports open 53 and blocked 14; --limit 3 reports open 4 and blocked 3; the canonical cold-start pm context --for orient reports open 4, blocked 3, and then prints total_items 2631, closed 2326, canceled 14 in the same summary block. One block therefore mixes two populations without saying so, and the intent AGENTS.md names as the measured cold-start tells a fresh agent that a 291-item backlog has four open items.\n\nThis is the read-output representativeness family applied to the summary itself: the part a bounded read returned claims a count for the part it withheld. Acceptance: summary counts are workspace-scoped (or the slice-scoped fields are renamed to say so, with the workspace count beside them); the orient and handoff intents carry both scopes explicitly; the omission receipt names summary as population-scoped; a negative control renders a slice count under a population key and fails; the truthful-context contract doc and the context intent fixtures record the field semantics."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:context",context-management,output-contracts,receipts,token-budget
